# 5. I would actually give every test a test ID

Something like:

```yaml
G-001:
  name: article_identification
  category: routing
  turns: 1

G-006:
  name: multi_hop_cross_reference
  category: legal_reasoning
  turns: 3

G-014:
  name: one_variable_scenario_mutation
  category: state_management
  turns: 5

G-020:
  name: effective_date_analysis
  category: temporal_law
  turns: 2

G-029:
  name: reciprocal_system
  category: cross_article
  turns: 4

G-030:
  name: full_end_to_end
  category: comprehensive
  turns: 20
```

Then after every change:

```text
Regression Run #27

Retrieval             98%
Article routing       100%
Applicability         94%
Recipe validation     91%
Calculation           100%
Scenario state        96%
Memory                98%
Cross-reference       89%
Adversarial           100%

Overall               95%
```

Even better, don't allow an overall score to hide critical failures.

For example:

```text
Overall: 95%

CRITICAL FAILURE:
G-023 Wrong Article injection
→ Article 12 provision incorrectly selected for Article 11 user
```

That should fail the deployment even though the overall score is high.

